# Salt Minion Configuration

## minion config

The main configuration file is `/etc/salt/minion`. It uses INI-style format for salt minion settings.

### Default Configuration

```ini
# Master configuration
master: salt

# Interface configuration
interface: 0.0.0.0
disable_ring: True

# Keepalive configuration
keepalive_interval: 30
keepalive_max_retries: 3

# Cache configuration
cache: file
compression: zlib

# Log configuration
log_level: info
log_file: /var/log/salt/minion

# Root directory
root_dir: /etc/salt
```

### Master Options

| Option | Description | Default |
|--------|-------------|---------|
| `master` | Salt master hostname/IP | - |
| `master_port` | Master port | 4505 |
| `mine` | Enable data minning | - |

### File Locations

| System | Config Path |
|--------|-------------|
| Linux (systemd) | `/etc/salt/minion` |
| Windows | `C:\salt\minion.conf` |

### Services Related

The salt minion works alongside:
- `salt-master` - The central coordination point
- `salt-api` - REST API for salt
- `salt-syndic` - Hierarchical salt deployment